      "critic": {
        "decision": "accept",
        "reason": "Bit-exact equivalence verified: for n = qh & 0xF, n * 0x02040810 = (n<<4)+(n<<11)+(n<<18)+(n<<25) with disjoint bit ranges (4-7, 11-14, 18-21, 25-28), so no carries; masking with 0x10101010 places bit0->4, bit1->12, bit2->20, bit3->28, matching the original vi0 mapping exactly, and the (qh>>16)&0xF variant reproduces the original vi1 mapping of qh bits 16-19. The hoisted vh >> (4*iqs) plus per-iteration >> (4*i) equals the original >> (4*(iqs+i)); arithmetic-shift sign bits are masked before use. Scale epilogue untouched. Governance: change confined to vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1 and vec_dot_q5_0_q8_1_impl in vecdotq.cuh, matching the manifest, cuda-vecdotq-v1 allowed symbols, and the arithmetic change class; no launch geometry touched, so no collision with dnr-q5-four-wave or any other DNR fingerprint; mechanism falls squarely under eligible hypothesis akh-v2-q5-type-specific-dequant. Expected dispatch lists the three sealed type-6 true/true anchors and correctly omits the 129-call false/true tail per the template's planner_target_exclusions. Diff context matches the sealed source preimage. Residual risk is low and self-falsifying: the impl signature change (const int * vh -> const int vh) would break compilation only if an out-of-manifest caller passed a pointer (current MMQ path converts Q5_0 tiles to Q8 and uses vec_dot_q8_0_q8_1_impl), and any such breakage fails at the build/correctness stage. Performance direction (constant multiply, possibly quarter-rate v_mul_lo_u32 on gfx90a, versus ~16 replaced shift/and/or ops per loop) is exactly what the declared falsifier and staged exact-kernel plus graphs-on screens will decide."
      },
